{"id":189584534767899,"type":"album","name":"E•MO•TION","artist":"Carly Rae Jepsen","year":2015,"weight":20,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/2015/34611-emotion-3.jpg","aoty":78,"aoty_user":85,"yt":"kV9sNmujCPk","links":{"aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/34611-carly-rae-jepsen-emotion.php"},"desc":"Emotion (stylized as E•MO•TION) is the third studio album by Canadian singer Carly Rae Jepsen. It was released on June 24, 2015 in Japan and on August 21, 2015 worldwide through 604, School Boy, and Interscope Records. Looking to transition from the \"pure pop\"-oriented nature of Kiss, Jepsen found inspiration in 1980s music and alternative styles. She enlisted a team of indie-pop collaborators including Dev Hynes, Ariel Rechtshaid and Rostam Batmanglij. Emotion received highly positive reviews from contemporary music critics, who placed the album on many year-end lists. Despite this, the album underperformed worldwide, debuting at number sixteen on the ."},"artist_ref":{"id":235175259843757,"name":"Carly Rae Jepsen","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Carly_Rae_Jepsen_%40_Troubadour_08_19_2025_%2854849754291%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":260819262438325,"type":"genre","name":"synth-pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":325,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":223122507869858,"type":"genre","name":"Dance-Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":311,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":19499532832736,"type":"genre","name":"Electropop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":265,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":266557216269112,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative R&B","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":241,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":204877716424121,"type":"genre","name":"Sophisti-Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":223,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":188582154918049,"type":"genre","name":"Synthwave","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":208,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":5763877178